course: dictionary
lesson: 3085
title: Educational
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Educational is an adjective. It describes something that teaches you or helps you learn. A visit to a science museum can be an educational trip, and a counting game can be an educational toy.
explain: Use the words around it to be sure. «An educational trip» is a day out where you learn something, and it can be fun too. The clue is that the thing is about learning, not just playing.
explain: The word also links to schools and teaching. «Educational system» means the way a country organises its schools. «Educational value» means how much a thing helps you learn.
explain: The example sentence says «special educational needs». Here educational is about learning and school. Ask yourself: is this thing for teaching? If yes, educational probably means helping you learn.
fact: Educational means teaching you something or helping you learn.
fact: «Educational toys» help children learn while they play.
fact: Educational can also mean connected with schools and teaching, as in «educational system».
fact: «Educational value» means how much a thing helps you learn.
fact: «Special educational needs» means extra help with learning.
exercise: The museum trip was very educational. What does educational mean here? | It was too long and boring | *It taught us something new | It was held in a school hall | It was cancelled because of rain
exercise: Which of these is an example of «educational toys»? | A kite for flying | *A set of letter blocks that help you spell | A teddy bear to cuddle | A ball for kicking outdoors
exercise: The example sentence says «special educational needs». What does educational mean in that phrase? | Connected with the sea | *Connected with learning and school | Connected with money | Connected with cooking
test: What does «educational value» mean? | *How much a thing helps you learn | How loud a thing is | How old a thing is | How much a thing costs
test: Which phrase is about schools and teaching? | A bag of sweets | *The educational system | A sunny beach | A pair of trainers
exam: Mum says the new TV show is very educational. What is she saying? | *It helps children learn something | It is funny and silly | It is too short to watch | It is only for grown-ups
